<title>USA: Magellan abandons well, to take charge.</title>
<headline>Magellan abandons well, to take charge.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON, Conn. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Magellan Petroleum Corporation said on Thursday that its Dogwood wildcat well in Colorado's Baca County has been plugged and abandoned at 4,623 feet after tests failed to recover any hydrocarbons.</p>
<p>The company said all remaining costs of the Baca County venture will be written off, as previously reported, resulting in an estimated after-tax charge of $1.1 million to net income in the fiscal fourth quarter ending June 30.</p>
<p>((-- David Chance New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
